<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                   http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.20.xsd">

    <!--
      Report, once, any MCP project linking an MCP server in one workspace to a project in another.

      createMcpProject never checked that the project belonged to the server's workspace, so such links could be
      created. Every MCP ownership resolver answers through the server, so for these rows MCP_VIEW in the server's
      workspace exposes the project's workflows to members with no access to the project's own workspace. New links
      are now refused where they are written.

      Existing rows are reported rather than changed. Which side is wrong - the server or the project - is a decision
      only an operator can make, and deleting the link would silently remove tools a running MCP client depends on.
      The precondition fails with WARN when any such row exists, which writes the warning to the startup log and lets
      the upgrade continue. The changeset itself changes nothing.

      To list the rows:

        SELECT mcp_project.id, workspace_mcp_server.workspace_id AS server_workspace_id,
               project.workspace_id AS project_workspace_id
        FROM mcp_project
                 JOIN workspace_mcp_server ON workspace_mcp_server.mcp_server_id = mcp_project.mcp_server_id
                 JOIN project_deployment ON project_deployment.id = mcp_project.project_deployment_id
                 JOIN project ON project.id = project_deployment.project_id
        WHERE workspace_mcp_server.workspace_id <> project.workspace_id;
    -->

    <changeSet id="20260914120000" author="Ivica Cardic">
        <preConditions onFail="WARN"
                       onFailMessage="Found MCP projects whose MCP server and project are in different workspaces. MCP_VIEW in the server's workspace exposes those projects' workflows. The query to list them is in 20260914120000_automation_mcp_report_cross_workspace_projects.xml.">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT COUNT(*)
                FROM mcp_project
                         JOIN workspace_mcp_server ON workspace_mcp_server.mcp_server_id = mcp_project.mcp_server_id
                         JOIN project_deployment ON project_deployment.id = mcp_project.project_deployment_id
                         JOIN project ON project.id = project_deployment.project_id
                WHERE workspace_mcp_server.workspace_id &lt;&gt; project.workspace_id
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>

        <comment>Report-only check for cross-workspace MCP projects. Changes nothing.</comment>

        <empty/>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
